@startuml
title TMFC009 : Service Qualification -- eTOM/SID ABE Links

' This diagram is genuinely a blank template in the source PDF, not a
' transcription gap: TMFC009.md section 2.2 (SID ABEs) has no data rows at
' all, only a note that a new Service Qualification SID BE still needs to be
' created. Both the eTOM activity and the SID entity are literally labelled
' "to be determined" in the source image -- reproduced verbatim rather than
' invented.
class "to be determined" as eTOMTBD <<eTOM Business Activity>>
class "to be determined" as SIDTBD <<SID Data Entity>>

' The source image draws a single squiggly connector between the two
' placeholder boxes with an arrowhead at BOTH ends (confirmed by zooming into
' the arrowhead region) -- unlike TMFC039/TMFC005's diagrams, which draw the
' "produces" and "is consumed by" relationships as two separate arrows. Since
' the entities themselves are unfilled placeholders, this is read as the
' template showing both of the legend's arrow meanings on the one connector,
' not as asserted real-world semantics.
eTOMTBD <--> SIDTBD

footer TMFC009 - Service Qualification (SID ABE not yet defined -- see section 2.2 note)

legend right
  an arrow from an eTOM activity towards a SID ABE means
  the information is produced by the activity;
  the arrow in the other direction means that the
  information is consumed by the activity
endlegend
@enduml
